Prompt: "{{PROMPT}}"
{{FROM_DIFF_NOTE}}
{{THIN_WARNING}}
{{CAPABILITY_BLOCK}}
{{DIFF_MATCHES}}

Execute in order, in a single linear pass:

1. Read the context pack and confirm (or correct) the capability:
       [[c]]doctrina context {{CAPABILITY}} --concat[[/c]]

2. If the capability has no spec yet:
       [[c]]doctrina spec new <capability>[[/c]]
[[g]]   Trace it to product intent: tag the product.md success-criteria bullet[[/g]]
[[g]]   it serves with an anchor ("- [SC1] ...") and set the spec's[[/g]]
[[g]]   "**Realizes:** SC1" header (or "n/a — <why>"). `doctrina validate` warns[[/g]]
[[g]]   on an active spec with no Realizes; `doctrina trace` reports the link.[[/g]]

{{STEP3_INTRO}}
[[g]]       # Spec Delta — capability: <capability>[[/g]]
[[g]]       **Operation:** ADDED | MODIFIED | REMOVED[[/g]]
[[g]]       **Target spec on apply:** `.doctrina/specs/<capability>/spec.md`[[/g]]
[[g]]       ---[[/g]]
[[g]]       <EARS body. Keep the two axes honest (Status vs Implementation),[[/g]]
[[g]]        keep aspiration under ## Maturity → Future, and cite the proof per[[/g]]
[[g]]        criterion: "1. [unverified] <signal> — verified by `path/to/test`">[[/g]]
[[g]]   New capability? `spec new` then an ADDED delta with the FULL body — apply[[/g]]
[[g]]   replaces the untouched scaffold. Bookkeeping edits? MODIFIED with an ops[[/g]]
[[g]]   block, applied mechanically (all ops or none):[[/g]]
[[g]]       ```ops[[/g]]
[[g]]       set-header Implementation: verified — `src/x.js`[[/g]]
[[g]]       bump-version minor[[/g]]
[[g]]       set-criterion 1: verified[[/g]]
[[g]]       append-criterion [unverified] new signal — verified by `test/y.test.js`[[/g]]
[[g]]       append-requirement event: When <trigger>, the system shall <action>.[[/g]]
[[g]]       replace-requirement ubiquitous 2: The system shall <action>.[[/g]]
[[g]]       ```[[/g]]
[[g]]   append-* ops number/position at APPLY time, so concurrent changes[[/g]]
[[g]]   appending to the same spec never collide. Only free-prose rewrites[[/g]]
[[g]]   (Purpose, Maturity, ...) stay a by-hand merge.[[/g]]
{{FROM_DIFF_DELTA_NOTE}}

4. Replace the placeholder tasks in .doctrina/changes/{{CHANGE_ID}}/tasks.md
   with small, checkable implementation tasks (a few hours each, max),
   and record the change's What/Scope in its proposal.md. Do this BEFORE
   implementing — analyze and close refuse a change whose scaffold
   placeholders were never replaced, and `change tick` will not tick them.

5. Implement task by task, checking each box as it lands. Advance the
   spec's Implementation: planned → partial → implemented as code lands.
   If the prompt is genuinely ambiguous, ask the user before assuming.

6. ADR checkpoint — does this change decide something structural
   (an architecture, a boundary, a trade-off a future session must
   not relitigate)? If yes: [[c]]doctrina decision new "<title>"[[/c]] now,
   before closing — the definition of done requires it recorded.
[[g]]   (close re-checks this: it warns when the change touches capabilities[[/g]]
[[g]]   cited by an accepted ADR — amend via decision supersede, not silence.)[[/g]]
   Touching an integration surface (ports, env vars, public endpoints)?
   Own it in a contract: [[c]]doctrina contract new <id>[[/c]] · [[c]]doctrina contract check[[/c]].

7. Close in one attested pass (preferred — runs every gate and stops
   at the first failure with the exact rerun command):
       [[c]]doctrina close {{CHANGE_ID}}[[/c]]
[[g]]   It self-reviews on the way through: the close runs `doctrina review`[[/g]]
[[g]]   before the apply, where its findings can still change what gets[[/g]]
[[g]]   written. Advisory — it reports and the close continues.[[/g]]
[[g]]   The sequence is declared in one place and printed by the close itself,[[/g]]
[[g]]   so read it there rather than from a copy that goes stale.[[/g]]
   Before it: check the proposal's ## Verification boxes and every task,
   closing steps included, and bump Implementation to verified.
   Two gates ask for WRITING, and both refuse late if you leave them:
   a change that alters a documented surface needs the documentation to
   move with it, AND an entry in the project's changelog — one says how it
   works, the other says that it changed. If the command and flag names in
   your prose are only MENTIONED, declare it instead of forcing:
   [[c]]- **Documented surface:** n/a — <why>[[/c]] in the proposal.

8. [[c]]doctrina next[[/c]] for the follow-up.
[[g]]   If this change taught a reusable lesson (a fix you'd hate to relearn,[[/g]]
[[g]]   a recurring convention), capture it: [[/g]][[c]]doctrina skill new <slug>[[/c]][[g]].[[/g]]
